delta-change "virtual-layout"
message "VirtualLayout: grammar-consumable virtual layout tokens"
author "ai"
doc "guide" """
  |# VirtualLayout: grammar-consumable virtual layout tokens
  |
  |VirtualLayout is a post-constitution Trellis product layered over SourceMapLayout. It does **not** extend or mutate the frozen F0–F11 bootstrap constitution.
  |
  |SourceMapLayout already derives deterministic `NEWLINE`, `INDENT`, and `DEDENT` events from the lossless source substrate. VirtualLayout closes the remaining semantic gap: those virtual events become ordinary first-class grammar expressions that the generic parser can consume.
  |
  |## Product identity
  |
  |```text
  |VirtualLayout.delta
  |4495bf6b9f2ff702344779733f55558bd2fdefd4790ae8621d51baa978ee1500
  |
  |VirtualLayout root
  |ff5505a8002973392efc9a9caa6d8c34b39dab85bc6669e9d509ed79544b273b
  |
  |503 nodes
  |707 edges
  |503 entities
  |```
  |
  |VirtualLayout depends exactly on SourceMapLayout.
  |
  |## Virtual layout terminals are graph entities
  |
  |VirtualLayout adds `grammar.layout-token` expressions. They do not contain textual spellings such as `"INDENT"`; instead each expression points to one of the layout-token entities introduced by SourceMapLayout:
  |
  |```text
  |grammar.bool0.g9.layout.newline ──grammar.layout-token──▶ layout.token.newline
  |grammar.bool0.g9.layout.indent  ──grammar.layout-token──▶ layout.token.indent
  |grammar.bool0.g9.layout.dedent  ──grammar.layout-token──▶ layout.token.dedent
  |```
  |
  |The layout policy also states how virtual and lexical tokens form one parser stream:
  |
  |```text
  |consumption   = grammar
  |stream-order  = byte-then-event
  |virtual-width = zero
  |```
  |
  |Virtual tokens therefore affect syntax but never pretend to occupy source bytes.
  |
  |## Block example
  |
  |VirtualLayout extends Bool0 with a layout-sensitive expression:
  |
  |```text
  |Block :=
  |  "block"
  |  NEWLINE
  |  INDENT
  |  capture-many(Expr NEWLINE)
  |  DEDENT
  |```
  |
  |For example:
  |
  |```text
  |block
  |  true
  |  !false
  |```
  |
  |parses to a `Block` tree whose `items` field has `many` cardinality and contains `True` and `Not(False)`.
  |
  |Canonical printing is driven by the same graph layout terminals:
  |
  |```text
  |block
  |  true
  |  ! false
  |```
  |
  |The canonical block surface ends with the final item `NEWLINE` consumed before `DEDENT`.
  |
  |## One semantic stream, two source views
  |
  |VirtualLayout preserves SourceProvenance/8's distinction between semantic syntax and source provenance:
  |
  |```text
  |source bytes
  |   │
  |   ├── lossless SourceDocument ──▶ exact original reconstruction
  |   │
  |   └── lexical tokens + virtual layout events ──▶ semantic parser
  |```
  |
  |Comments and whitespace remain real source trivia. `NEWLINE`, `INDENT`, and `DEDENT` are virtual zero-width parser tokens. Consuming them cannot destroy source reconstruction.
  |
  |## Compatibility
  |
  |A one-line SourceMapLayout expression such as:
  |
  |```text
  |π&&0007
  |```
  |
  |still parses and normalizes identically under VirtualLayout:
  |
  |```text
  |π && 7
  |```
  |
  |The final root-level `NEWLINE` event is not injected into the semantic stream when it is merely the terminal event of a one-line expression. This preserves the pre-layout surface while retaining layout events in `layoutSource`.
  |
  |## Free changes
  |
  |`DeltaBool0` is extended so the graph-defined replace/remove operators admit `grammar.layout-token` entities. Layout-policy edits also flow through the existing free DeltaTrellis specialization.
  |
  |For example, changing `indent-unit` from `2` to `4` changes which block sources parse without modifying host parser code.
  |
  |Invalid stream policy edits fail closed. A layout9 policy must retain:
  |
  |```text
  |consumption   = grammar
  |stream-order  = byte-then-event
  |virtual-width = zero
  |```
  |
  |## Deliberate boundary
  |
  |VirtualLayout demonstrates flat offside suites. Arbitrarily nested layout-sensitive suites are intentionally not claimed yet: ownership of the newline around a nested suite boundary needs its own statement/suite structure rather than an implicit parser preference. A later product slice should model that boundary explicitly.
  |
  """
test "canonical delta contract"
  assert "canonical"
  assert "valid"
  assert "source-roundtrip"
  assert "dependency" "source-maps-layout"
  assert "introduces" "grammar.component.layout-token" "grammar.component"
